<script>
  import ThemedShot from '$lib/components/changelog/ThemedShot.svelte';
</script>

This June source milestone added a **design-system list and picker**, a
freeform model route and image-URL path, and optional **model-assisted prop
inference** for constrained generation. Scanned systems and projects can be
stored in a JSON-backed file store. A component linter can flag generated
component names that are absent from the supplied library. The work also
updated model-provider configuration and source tooling.

Matching still uses keyword scoring. Generated code, suggested props,
accessibility checks, and tests need validation in the target project. This
milestone does not establish first-pass PR acceptance, provider parity, or
production readiness.

The previous light/dark home stills are withdrawn from this entry because
their visible “production-ready code” promise exceeds that evidence. A
separate, dated study of the actual Svelte/Vue scanner appears below; it is
not June milestone footage or a replacement film.


## Current source-run scanner study · September 25, 2026

These paired light/dark captures come from the **actual locally run Compokit
API and web app** with isolated synthetic Svelte and Vue component libraries.
They show a later source state, not the June milestone. The API readback found
one component and two CSS tokens in each disposable library. The app's form
and result views were captured through its local design-system workflow.
No public scanner account, hosted generation service, model-quality result,
or production target project is demonstrated.

The [public Compokit source overview](https://aylith-labs.github.io/compokit/)
is a static explanation of scan → keyword match → reviewable generation, not
a hosted product app or an installation route.

